<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.8.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01393</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.8.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>269ed262-bc2e-4cf0-8b54-3630742ec1c6</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001">

        <exercise id="_54e1ee56-0684-4f78-9d2e-b434955a8f28" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00001">
            <para id="para-00001">For an experiment, a scientist designs a can, 20 cm in height, that holds water. A tube is installed at the bottom of the can allowing water to drain out.</para>
          <para id="para-00002">At the beginning of the experiment, the can is full. Every minute after the start of the experiment, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math> of the water is drained.</para>
          <para id="para-00003">The height of the water, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, in cm, is a function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> of time <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> in minutes since the
            beginning of the experiment, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>. Which is an expression for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
      
            <para id="para-00004">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00005"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00006"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00007"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00008"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            
            <para id="para-00009">Try again. Revisit activities 5.8.2 – 5.8.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00010">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>.
    </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="cdc0de8f-f7ad-4b24-a42e-b6c7217de1fa" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00002">
            <para id="para-00011">A bacteria population is 10,000. It triples each day. The bacteria population, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, is a function of
          the number of days, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>. Which equation relates <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
            <para id="para-00012">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00013"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>10000</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>d</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00014"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>10000</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>d</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00015"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>10000</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mi>d</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00016"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>10000</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>d</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
          <solution id="sol-00002">
            
            <para id="para-00017">Try again. Revisit activities 5.8.2 – 5.8.4 to test your understanding? Then come
        back and try this question again.</para>
            <para id="para-00018">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>10000</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>d</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>.
    </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_0b3534d1-9dcd-4d60-b28a-7553f9e04c3c" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00003">
            <para id="para-00019">The area, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, covered by a city is 20 square miles. The area grows by a factor of 1.1 each year, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>,
          since it was 20 square miles. Which equation expresses <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> in terms of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
            <para id="para-00020">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00021"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>1.1</m:mn><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00022"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mn>1.1</m:mn><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00023"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>1.1</m:mn><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00024"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>1.1</m:mn><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
          <solution id="sol-00003">
            
            <para id="para-00025">Try again. Revisit activities 5.8.2 – 5.8.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00026">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>1.1</m:mn><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>.
    </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_5778ce9d-a0fd-4fb0-ab3a-3b9bae8a95dc" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00004">
            <para id="para-00027">The graph below models the water draining out of a tube during an experiment represented by the function, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>/</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>.
          What does the value <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>20</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math>) mean in the context of the problem? (<media alt=""><image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_10_10_01.jpg"/></media>)</para>
            <para id="para-00028">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00029">After 2 minutes, the height of the water is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>20</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math> centimeters less than at the start.</para>
            <para id="para-00030">After <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>20</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math> minutes, the height of the water is 2 centimeters.</para>
            <para id="para-00031">After 2 minutes, the height of the water is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>20</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math> centimeters.</para>
            <para id="para-00032">After <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>20</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math> minutes, the height of the water is 2 centimeters less than at the start.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00004">
            
            <para id="para-00033">Try again. Revisit activities 5.8.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00034">The correct answer is: After 2 minutes, the height of the water is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>20</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math> centimeters.
    </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_55059bdc-fd74-48e4-855f-94fcbe04bbe3" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00005">
            <para id="para-00035">A scientist measures the height, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, of a tree each month, and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is the number of months since the
          scientist first measured the height of the tree. Is the height, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, a function of the month, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>?
      </para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00005">
            
            <para id="para-00036">Try again. Revisit activity 5.8.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00037">The correct answer is: Yes because the scientist measures the height of the tree each month and gets a value,
        so for each value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, there will be a height <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_720112a8-813a-4511-bc7c-4bf5a1f76b02" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00006">
            <para id="para-00038">Cary started with 3 goldfish in her tank, and the population doubled every month. Which is an equation that
          represents the population, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>P</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, of goldfish after <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> months?
      </para>
            <para id="para-00039">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00040"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>P</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00041"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>P</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00042"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>P</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00043"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>P</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
          <solution id="sol-00006">
            
            <para id="para-00044">Try again. Revisit activities 5.8.2 – 5.8.4 to test your understanding? Then come
        back and try this question again.</para>
            <para id="para-00045">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>P</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>.
    </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_1c91e30d-674a-4571-92ed-4e12263bbee2" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00007">
            <para id="para-00046">Use this equation for problems 7 – 10:
        <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>50</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00047">What is the initial value?</para>
            
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00007">
            <para id="para-00048">Correct! The initial value is 50. When
        <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>50</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>50</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>50</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00049">Try again. Revisit activity 5.8.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00050">The correct answer is: The initial value is 50. When
        <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>,<m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>50</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>50</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>50</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="e40d2def-b7bf-4139-8f97-ed505f105823" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00008">
            
            <para id="para-00051">What is the growth factor?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00008">
            <para id="para-00052">Correct! The initial value is 2. The growth factor refers to the constant multiplier that determines how the
        function grows or decays as the independent variable changes. In this equation, the growth factor is 2.</para>
            <para id="para-00053">Try again. Revisit activity 5.8.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00054">The correct answer is: The initial value is 2. The growth factor refers to the constant multiplier that
        determines how the function grows or decays as the independent variable changes. In this equation, the growth
        factor is 2.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_8b18c59d-a4c8-4193-b9a3-f29c1675d9f2" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00009">
            <para id="para-00055">What is the independent variable?
      </para>
            <para id="para-00056">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00057"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00058"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
          <solution id="sol-00009">
            <para id="para-00059">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, The independent variable is the variable that is manipulated or controlled and is represented by
        <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> in this equation.</para>
            <para id="para-00060">Try again. Revisit activity 5.8.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00061">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, The independent variable is the variable that is manipulated or controlled and is
        represented by <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> in this equation.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_0e063d30-b916-44a4-b667-c051bafdbcb0" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00010">
            <para id="para-00062">What is the dependent variable?
      </para>
            <para id="para-00063">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00064"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00065"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
          <solution id="sol-00010">
            <para id="para-00066">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, The dependent variable is the variable that depends on or is influenced by the independent variable. In this
        equation, the dependent variable is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, which represents the output or value of the function.</para>
            <para id="para-00067">Try again. Revisit activity 5.8.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00068"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, The dependent variable is the variable that depends on or is influenced by the independent variable. In
        this equation, the dependent variable is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, which represents the output or value of the function.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="cb878148-c8cb-464b-9a7d-cfe8d9def838" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00011">
            <para id="para-00069">Which equation is most appropriate for modeling this data?</para>
            <table class="unnumbered os-raise-horizontaltable" id="table-00001">
              <tgroup cols="7"><tbody><row>
                  <entry>
                   <emphasis>x</emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>1</entry>
                  <entry>2</entry>
                  <entry>3</entry>
                  <entry>4</entry>
                  <entry>5</entry>
                  <entry>6</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>
                   <emphasis>y</emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>50</entry>
                  <entry>100</entry>
                  <entry>200</entry>
                  <entry>400</entry>
                  <entry>800</entry>
                  <entry>1600</entry>
                </row>
              </tbody></tgroup></table>
            <para id="para-00070">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00071"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>25</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00072"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>25</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00073"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>25</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00074"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>50</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
          <solution id="sol-00011">
            <para id="para-00075">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>25</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00076">Try again. Revisit activity 5.8.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00077">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>25</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

    </section>
